      "description": {
        "fun": "Zigzagoon can't walk in a straight line: it wanders restlessly back and forth, nose to the ground, leaving zigzag footprints, and it's good at picking up lost items. It plays dead to fool opponents. Ken Sugimori says its name came before its design, and its family tells a little story of movement: Zigzagoon zigzags, Linoone runs straight, and Obstagoon blocks the way.",
        "guide": "A Normal-type, raccoon-like Pokémon with zigzag-patterned fur that wanders in zigzags and picks up items. It evolves into Linoone at level 20. Its Dark- and Normal-type Galarian form, thought to be the original, evolves through Galarian Linoone into Obstagoon.",
